# Existing Features &amp; Source Notes

> **Project**: 	elegrambots — Multi-bot GitHub → Telegram notification platform
> **Architecture**: Clean Architecture (Onion) + Pipeline Pattern + Rich Domain Model
> **Stack**: Java 21 · Spring Boot 4 · MongoDB · Docker · ngrok

---

## 1. Domain Layer (	elegrambots-domain)

### 1.1 Entities (Rich Domain Model)

| Class | Location | Description |
|---|---|---|
| ManagedBot | domain/bot/ManagedBot.java | Core entity: token, username, githubRepo, webhook secrets, enabled flag. Contains factory create() and mutation merge(BotRegistration) with direct invariant checks. |
| GroupActivation | domain/activation/GroupActivation.java | Binding entity: this bot is allowed to send to this chat. Validated on construction. State-mutating methods: ctivate() / deactivate(). |
| ActivationResult | domain/activation/ActivationResult.java | Value object returned by activation: carries the saved GroupActivation plus 
ewlyActivated flag. |

### 1.2 Value Objects &amp; Shared

| Class | Location | Description |
|---|---|---|
| BotUsername | domain/shared/BotUsername.java | Normalizes @ prefix for consistent lookup keys. |
| MessageFormatter | domain/shared/MessageFormatter.java | HTML formatting helpers (code(), etc.) for Telegram messages. |
| BotRegistration | domain/bot/BotRegistration.java | Immutable input DTO for creating / updating a bot. Nullable fields = partial update semantics. |

### 1.3 Domain Events

| Class | Location | Description |
|---|---|---|
| BotSavedEvent | domain/bot/BotSavedEvent.java | Published when a bot is created or updated (carries token, username, enabled flag). |
| BotDeletedEvent | domain/bot/BotDeletedEvent.java | Published when a bot is deleted. Triggers webhook de-registration. |

### 1.4 Pipeline Abstraction

| Class | Location | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Pipeline<C, R> | domain/pipeline/Pipeline.java | Generic sequential pipeline: runs a list of Step until one short-circuits with a result. Accepts List<? extends Step<C,R>> for covariant step injection. |
| Step<C, R> | domain/pipeline/Step.java | Single-method interface: Optional<R> execute(C context). Empty = continue; present = short-circuit. |

