## 4. Web Layer (	elegrambots-web)

### 4.1 Admin REST API

Base path: /admin/bots — all endpoints require X-Admin-Token header.

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| /admin/bots | GET | List all bots. |
| /admin/bots/{username} | GET | Find single bot. Returns 404 if not found. |
| /admin/bots | POST | Create or update bot (username from request body). |
| /admin/bots/{username} | PUT | Update bot (username from URL path overrides body). |
| /admin/bots/{username} | DELETE | Delete bot + all activations + de-register webhook. |

Supporting classes:

| Class | Location | Description |
|---|---|---|
| AdminAccessGuard | dmin/impl/AdminAccessGuard.java | Validates X-Admin-Token header. Returns 403 if token mismatch. |
| AdminBotService | dmin/impl/AdminBotService.java | Thin service: delegates to BotManagementUseCase, maps via AdminBotMapper. |
| AdminBotMapper | dmin/impl/AdminBotMapper.java | Maps ManagedBot to/from AdminBotResponse DTO. |
| AdminBotRequest | dmin/dto/AdminBotRequest.java | Request DTO with 	oRegistration(usernameOverride) factory. |
| AdminBotResponse | dmin/dto/AdminBotResponse.java | Response DTO (masks token, exposes hasToken flag). |

### 4.2 Telegram Webhook Pipeline

Entry: POST /telegram/webhook/{botUsername}

| # | Step | Description |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | TelegramSecretVerificationStep | Validates X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token header. |
| 2 | TelegramBotLookupStep | Loads enabled bot from cache. |
| 3 | TelegramMessageValidationStep | Validates update has a text message. |
| 4 | TelegramCommandParsingStep | Extracts command token and arg from message text. |
| 5 | TelegramCommandLookupStep | Matches command text to registered BotCommand beans. |
| 6 | TelegramCommandExecutionStep | Calls BotCommand.execute(); sends reply via TelegramGateway. |

### 4.3 Telegram Bot Commands

All commands implement BotCommand (	elegram/command/BotCommand.java).

| Command | Class | Description |
|---|---|---|
| /add @bot | AddCommand | Renders `GroupActivationCommandResult` from the application layer. |
| /remove @bot | RemoveCommand | Renders `GroupActivationCommandResult` from the application layer. |
| /status | StatusCommand | Queries isActive + ctiveGroupCount; formats status card. |
| /id | IdCommand | Returns chatId of current group. |
| /start | StartCommand | Greeting message. |
| /help | HelpCommand | Lists all available commands with syntax. |

### 4.4 GitHub Webhook Pipeline

Entry: POST /github/webhook/{botUsername}

| # | Step | Description |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | SignatureVerificationStep | Validates X-Hub-Signature-256 HMAC-SHA256. |
| 2 | BotLookupStep | Loads enabled bot from cache. |
| 3 | JsonParsingStep | Parses raw body to JsonNode. |
| 4 | PingCheckStep | Short-circuits with PING_OK for GitHub ping events. |
| 5 | EventPresenceStep | Validates X-GitHub-Event header presence. |
| 6 | RepositoryMatchStep | Checks 
epository.full_name matches bot's githubRepo. |
| 7 | EventExecutionStep | Renders the matching event formatter and broadcasts non-empty messages. |

### 4.5 GitHub Event Formatters

Each formatter supports exactly one GitHub event type. `GitHubEventRenderer` selects the formatter, and `EventExecutionStep` broadcasts formatted HTML via `BroadcastUseCase`.

| Event Type | Formatter | Formatter Output |
|---|---|---|
| push | PushEventFormatter | Branch name, commit count, committer, commit list. |
| star | StarEventFormatter | Starred / unstarred by user. |
| issues | IssueEventFormatter | Opened / closed / edited issue. |
| pull_request | PullRequestEventFormatter | Opened / merged / closed PR. |
| issue_comment | IssueCommentEventFormatter | New comment on issue or PR. |
| workflow_run | WorkflowRunEventFormatter | CI pipeline completed (success / failure). |
| release | ReleaseEventFormatter | Published release with tag name and release notes. |

